FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: joinder.

OFF THE RECORD: a case that opens another case. The new filing is an
OFF THE RECORD: ordinary string (newlines are whitespace, so a whole
OFF THE RECORD: Form K-1 fits in one); COMMENCE files it with the
OFF THE RECORD: court and records the case number it earns. The
OFF THE RECORD: parent then introduces itself by serving its own case
OFF THE RECORD: number, and the two correspond like any other pair.

ARTICLE 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT charter IS
        "FORM K-1. IN THE MATTER OF: the-junior-party. ARTICLE 1. AWAIT SUMMONS, FILED UNDER counterparty. SERVE NOTICE OF \"the junior party appears\" UPON counterparty. ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.".
    COMMENCE PROCEEDINGS UPON charter, FILED UNDER junior.

ARTICLE 2.
    SERVE NOTICE OF THE CASE AT BAR UPON junior.
    AWAIT SUMMONS, FILED UNDER appearance.
    PROCLAIM appearance.
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.
